quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  16,43,"And We did not send (any messenger) before you, except men to whom We had revealed. Ask the People of the Reminder if you do not know."
  16,44,"(We sent them) with clear proofs and Scriptures. And (Esteemed Prophet,) We have revealed the Reminder (i.e. the Qur’an) to you so that you may clearly explain to the people what has been sent down to them; perhaps they may reflect."
  16,45,"Do those who have plotted evil deeds feel secure that Allah will not cause the earth to swallow them, or the punishment will not overtake them (suddenly) from where they do not perceive?"
  16,46,"Or that He will not seize them during their journeys, then they will not be able to escape?"
  16,47,"Or that He will not seize them with gradual attrition (striking them with fear)? Indeed, your Lord is Most-Kind, All-Merciful."
  16,48,"Have they not considered that whatever Allah has created casts its shadow to the right and the left, prostrating to Allah in utter humility?"
  16,49,"To Allah prostrates whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth from the living creatures, as do the angels, who are not arrogant."
  16,50,They fear their Lord above them and do what they are commanded.
  16,51,"And Allah has said: ‘Do not take two gods. Truly, He is only One God. So you should be afraid of Me alone.’"
  16,52,To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. And to Him belongs the everlasting devotion. Will you then be conscious of something other than Allah?
  16,53,"And whatever blessing you possess comes from Allah. Then, whenever hardship afflicts you, to Him (alone), you cry (for help)."
  16,54,"Yet, when He removes the hardship from you, a group of you attribute partners to your Lord,"
